{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And Abram</b> was born in a place called Ur of the Chaldees, and like it: therefore in the Urim glorify HaShem (Isaiah 24:15). And it is likely that it had another name there, for the Chaldees are of the descendants of Nahor, Abram's brother; only Moses wrote the name known in his days. And the proof that Abram was born there is that Haran his brother died there, and it is written: in the land of his birth. It is also possible that the Chaldees made light (אור) in that mentioned place, and it was called thus, like \"who has light (אור) in Zion\" (Isaiah 1:9)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The second Isaiah verse cited (1:9) does not contain the quoted phrase 'אשר אור לו בציון'; the citation or verse number may be corrupt in the source text. Translated hyper-literally as printed."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:17.724120359Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}